1
00:02:44,231 --> 00:02:46,499
Another double?

2
00:02:49,303 --> 00:02:51,003
Let's go
- Yes

3
00:02:57,110 --> 00:03:01,013
Did that old man Honjo use another decoy?

4
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:03,171
Sorry, Boss

5
00:03:03,751 --> 00:03:05,351
We failed

6
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,589
Once that old man is gone...

7
00:03:10,457 --> 00:03:12,792
this city will be mine

8
00:03:13,627 --> 00:03:17,763
You've been telling me that since we were young

9
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:22,835
I will make you the top boss in Japan

10
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:24,604
Excuse me

11
00:03:26,507 --> 00:03:28,207
The car is ready

12
00:03:41,989 --> 00:03:44,323
We must eliminate him

13
00:04:07,481 --> 00:04:10,082
Honjo barely shows his face in public

14
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:12,318
Just how many doubles does he have?

15
00:04:12,319 --> 00:04:14,153
The man is incredibly cautious

16
00:04:15,189 --> 00:04:17,990
That's how he stayed at the top

17
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,327
Big Brother

18
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,329
Yeah, what?

19
00:04:23,730 --> 00:04:26,766
My daughter takes classes at a dance studio

20
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,334
So?

21
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:31,604
I dropped her off for my wife yesterday...

22
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:33,406
and guess what I saw there?

23
00:04:33,407 --> 00:04:36,242
A girl being picked up in a luxury sedan

24
00:04:38,846 --> 00:04:40,112
We're here

25
00:04:45,853 --> 00:04:47,587
What kind of dance is it today?

26
00:04:47,588 --> 00:04:48,454
Hip-hop

27
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:50,590
Sounds cool!

28
00:04:50,591 --> 00:04:51,290
Here

29
00:04:59,566 --> 00:05:01,434
And here too
- Okay

30
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:04,103
You got this?
- Yeah

31
00:05:08,408 --> 00:05:10,265
Thanks for the ride, Grandpa

32
00:05:10,289 --> 00:05:11,444
I'm off!

33
00:05:15,249 --> 00:05:17,583
Miku!
- Shiori!

34
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,953
Your hair looks so cute today!

35
00:05:25,092 --> 00:05:26,125
Bye bye

36
00:05:28,562 --> 00:05:29,996
Bye!

37
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:37,762
You idiot!

38
00:05:37,786 --> 00:05:39,572
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

39
00:05:39,907 --> 00:05:40,773
I'm sorry

40
00:05:42,276 --> 00:05:44,042
I'm sure of it

41
00:05:44,066 --> 00:05:45,678
That was Honjo

42
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:49,282
And look at this

43
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,789
It's for my daughter's dance competition

44
00:05:56,957 --> 00:05:58,858
Honjo's granddaughter enters every year

45
00:05:58,859 --> 00:06:00,660
I heard she's won several times

46
00:06:02,029 --> 00:06:04,530
The Dance Grand Koshien

47
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,700
Honjo absolutely dotes on his granddaughter

48
00:06:07,868 --> 00:06:10,837
It's the only place he shows up to watch

49
00:06:12,105 --> 00:06:16,042
Take your family and leave Tokyo for a while

50
00:06:16,643 --> 00:06:18,834
If word gets out,

51
00:06:18,858 --> 00:06:20,479
you're dead

52
00:06:44,204 --> 00:06:47,039
Why the hell did you call me to a place like this?

53
00:06:50,210 --> 00:06:51,644
You and me...

54
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:55,248
two freelance hitmen in the same room?

55
00:06:57,317 --> 00:07:00,853
You're Kumashiro from the Kazama Faction, right?

56
00:07:01,321 --> 00:07:03,690
Why gather so many hitmen here?

57
00:07:04,026 --> 00:07:05,200
Trying to get us to kill each other?

58
00:07:05,225 --> 00:07:06,926
You talk too much

59
00:07:09,329 --> 00:07:11,330
I'll take you out first

60
00:07:15,402 --> 00:07:18,004
Of course it'd turn out like this

61
00:07:27,214 --> 00:07:30,550
Is this some kind of hitman reunion?

62
00:07:30,551 --> 00:07:31,536
Fine

63
00:07:31,985 --> 00:07:33,886
Let's see who's the best

64
00:07:34,588 --> 00:07:36,756
I'm retired

65
00:07:39,793 --> 00:07:41,761
Cut the crap

66
00:08:30,644 --> 00:08:31,700
Hello?

67
00:08:33,524 --> 00:08:35,541
Just leave the package at the front gate

68
00:08:40,486 --> 00:08:41,620
It's the delivery guy

69
00:08:47,995 --> 00:08:49,795
What's with those faces?

70
00:08:49,997 --> 00:08:51,464
Cut it out

71
00:08:54,001 --> 00:08:57,336
I didn't call you here to kill each other

72
00:08:58,278 --> 00:09:00,279
I have a job for you

73
00:09:01,642 --> 00:09:05,545
Like I said, I'm out of the game

74
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:08,314
Besides, I don't work with people I can't trust

75
00:09:08,315 --> 00:09:10,850
You guys are the only ones who can pull this off

76
00:09:12,452 --> 00:09:14,954
I want you to form a dance crew

77
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:18,291
A dance crew?

78
00:09:18,574 --> 00:09:23,539
I did some research, you all have dance experience

79
00:09:23,564 --> 00:09:25,665
That was a long time ago

80
00:09:25,666 --> 00:09:27,633
Better than nothing

81
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:33,372
You took dance classes in elementary school, right?

82
00:09:34,007 --> 00:09:36,475
And you won several championships

83
00:09:42,883 --> 00:09:45,218
Thank you
- Thank you, everyone

84
00:10:10,377 --> 00:10:11,878
What are you doing?

85
00:10:15,349 --> 00:10:20,586
And you joined a community dance class

86
00:10:40,908 --> 00:10:43,643
It was a folk dance club for local residents

87
00:10:45,078 --> 00:10:46,979
Dance is dance

88
00:10:49,316 --> 00:10:52,151
Your background is especially impressive

89
00:10:52,786 --> 00:10:55,221
Your mother was a famous ballerina

90
00:10:55,722 --> 00:10:59,725
And you won multiple competitions yourself

91
00:11:02,625 --> 00:11:04,831
- Daiya, point your toes more!
- Yes

92
00:11:09,002 --> 00:11:10,403
Your toes are too low

93
00:11:10,404 --> 00:11:13,406
- You won't win the competition like that
- Yes

94
00:11:13,407 --> 00:11:15,007
Are you even listening to me?

95
00:11:15,475 --> 00:11:16,475
Yes

96
00:11:16,777 --> 00:11:17,743
Again

97
00:11:23,150 --> 00:11:24,139
I...

98
00:11:26,487 --> 00:11:27,820
hate dancing

99
00:11:28,755 --> 00:11:30,078
This is ridiculous

100
00:11:30,102 --> 00:11:31,324
I'm out

101
00:11:33,627 --> 00:11:37,430
If we succeed, it's 100 million yen each

102
00:11:41,962 --> 00:11:42,942
I told you...

103
00:11:44,638 --> 00:11:47,033
I'm not a hitman anymore

104
00:12:45,399 --> 00:12:46,521
You're back

105
00:12:47,134 --> 00:12:48,167
I'm home

106
00:12:50,504 --> 00:12:53,539
Everyone here is so close

107
00:12:53,874 --> 00:12:57,777
It's heartbreaking to split them up

108
00:12:58,078 --> 00:13:00,046
Isn't there any other way?

109
00:13:00,581 --> 00:13:03,950
It's the landowner's decision, so we're sorry

110
00:13:04,251 --> 00:13:06,519
These are the related documents

111
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:08,788
Please review them

112
00:13:09,957 --> 00:13:13,426
We'll take our leave now

113
00:13:22,369 --> 00:13:23,269
Excuse us

114
00:13:27,774 --> 00:13:31,744
Should we try appealing to the government?

115
00:13:32,079 --> 00:13:33,312
It's no use

116
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:37,550
The landlord wants to build luxury high-rises here

117
00:13:39,419 --> 00:13:42,221
What about the kids?

118
00:13:43,423 --> 00:13:44,790
At this rate...

119
00:13:45,058 --> 00:13:49,729
we'll have to send them to different facilities

120
00:14:00,607 --> 00:14:02,575
Then we'll just have to buy the place

121
00:14:03,076 --> 00:14:04,166
Buy it?

122
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:05,667
With what?

123
00:14:05,691 --> 00:14:07,580
That's a fortune

124
00:14:07,814 --> 00:14:11,150
It's a pipe dream

125
00:14:15,515 --> 00:14:16,908
Sorry...

126
00:14:16,932 --> 00:14:17,917
Dai

127
00:14:17,948 --> 00:14:19,525
You're just a part-timer...

128
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,427
but we're making you worry

129
00:14:22,329 --> 00:14:23,830
I'm home

130
00:14:25,632 --> 00:14:26,632
Welcome back

131
00:14:27,968 --> 00:14:29,248
I'm home!

132
00:14:29,272 --> 00:14:30,703
I'm starving

133
00:14:30,704 --> 00:14:32,271
I'll get dinner ready right away

134
00:14:32,506 --> 00:14:34,373
Wash your hands first

135
00:14:38,697 --> 00:14:40,113
Hey, Dai

136
00:14:40,459 --> 00:14:41,480
Yeah?

137
00:14:42,216 --> 00:14:44,884
Do you ever find life exhausting?

138
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:50,656
Asuka, why are you talking like an old man?

139
00:14:52,192 --> 00:14:54,216
I'm almost ten

140
00:14:54,795 --> 00:14:57,029
I think about things

141
00:14:57,865 --> 00:14:59,632
Like my future

142
00:15:01,301 --> 00:15:02,502
I see

143
00:15:11,678 --> 00:15:13,579
Tell me what's on your mind

144
00:15:14,882 --> 00:15:15,871
I...

145
00:15:16,643 --> 00:15:18,911
want to go pro...

146
00:15:19,219 --> 00:15:21,854
Yeah
- but it's not that simple

147
00:15:22,089 --> 00:15:24,524
Maybe I should just face reality

148
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:30,830
I think chasing your dreams is important

149
00:15:31,899 --> 00:15:35,935
That's what adults say...

150
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:38,771
but the reality is different

151
00:15:39,673 --> 00:15:42,508
The economy is in a slump...

152
00:15:43,443 --> 00:15:45,411
and there's the declining birthrate and aging population

153
00:16:14,441 --> 00:16:15,641
This is the contract

154
00:16:16,143 --> 00:16:18,377
[Target Heizo Honjo,
Do not betray your partners]

155
00:16:18,378 --> 00:16:20,546
[Practice diligently,
Keep this contract confidential]

156
00:16:20,547 --> 00:16:22,114
[Reward 100,000,000 Yen]

157
00:16:27,221 --> 00:16:28,554
I have one condition

158
00:16:30,791 --> 00:16:32,124
What is it?

159
00:16:33,727 --> 00:16:35,728
You have to join the team too

160
00:16:39,466 --> 00:16:41,267
I don't know how to dance

161
00:16:42,436 --> 00:16:44,536
I've always worked alone

162
00:16:45,339 --> 00:16:47,306
I don't trust anyone

163
00:16:49,343 --> 00:16:52,612
I need to be close enough
to kill you if you betray me

164
00:16:53,113 --> 00:16:55,014
So you're dancing with us

165
00:17:05,025 --> 00:17:06,459
Fine

166
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:17,136
Our target is Heizo Honjo, boss of the Honjo Association

167
00:17:19,772 --> 00:17:22,942
He is incredibly cautious...

168
00:17:23,677 --> 00:17:26,345
but our chance is coming

169
00:17:30,450 --> 00:17:32,151
Every year, he attends the finals of

170
00:17:32,152 --> 00:17:35,988
his granddaughter's dance competition

171
00:17:36,523 --> 00:17:39,792
So, you're making us dance

172
00:17:39,793 --> 00:17:41,160
to sneak into the venue?

173
00:17:41,161 --> 00:17:44,730
Honjo is vigilant but he lets his guard down

174
00:17:44,965 --> 00:17:47,567
around his granddaughter

175
00:17:47,801 --> 00:17:50,303
That's the only place he doesn't use a double

176
00:17:51,371 --> 00:17:52,682
He sits in the front row

177
00:17:52,707 --> 00:17:56,409
right where he can see her best

178
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:10,723
A shot from the stage will definitely kill him

179
00:18:11,258 --> 00:18:13,025
And getting away will be easy

180
00:18:13,594 --> 00:18:17,697
I believe I mentioned that I hate dancing

181
00:18:19,266 --> 00:18:21,567
You're dancing whether you like it or not

182
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:25,271
We have less than six months until the competition

183
00:18:25,539 --> 00:18:27,740
We must pass the qualifiers no matter what

184
00:18:29,042 --> 00:18:29,965
First...

185
00:18:30,911 --> 00:18:33,579
I need to see what you can do

186
00:18:45,359 --> 00:18:46,759
Good morning, everyone

187
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:47,927
Good morning

188
00:18:47,961 --> 00:18:50,196
This is the beginner jazz class

189
00:18:50,197 --> 00:18:53,065
First, let's do the pony step

190
00:18:53,066 --> 00:18:54,867
Put your weight on your left foot

191
00:18:57,771 --> 00:18:59,906
Raise your right foot

192
00:19:04,645 --> 00:19:06,832
Add the arms

193
00:19:06,856 --> 00:19:07,980
Stretch them out to the sides

194
00:19:09,651 --> 00:19:10,883
Up!

195
00:19:10,884 --> 00:19:13,219
Right hand, left hand

196
00:19:13,253 --> 00:19:15,721
Both arms out and up

197
00:19:15,756 --> 00:19:17,957
Right hand, left hand

198
00:19:17,991 --> 00:19:20,159
Extend and up

199
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,428
Right hand, left hand

200
00:19:30,971 --> 00:19:32,405
Your hands are too close

201
00:19:37,010 --> 00:19:38,146
That's the wrong move

202
00:19:38,170 --> 00:19:39,478
Don't mess up

203
00:19:46,854 --> 00:19:50,022
Okay next is a basic jazz step, the single turn

204
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:51,190
Start with your right foot

205
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,401
Right side!

206
00:19:57,365 --> 00:19:58,728
Left side!

207
00:20:02,302 --> 00:20:03,291
Left side!

208
00:20:05,807 --> 00:20:07,440
Next!

209
00:20:25,492 --> 00:20:26,659
Are you okay?

210
00:20:29,129 --> 00:20:30,101
Next!

211
00:20:51,585 --> 00:20:53,152
I hate dancing

212
00:20:53,153 --> 00:20:54,318
Next!

213
00:20:59,092 --> 00:21:01,761
Hey, do it right!

214
00:21:03,397 --> 00:21:04,864
Don't order me around

215
00:21:05,199 --> 00:21:06,732
Here they go again

216
00:21:30,791 --> 00:21:31,924
Stop it!

217
00:21:34,695 --> 00:21:40,032
Sensei, we really want to learn how to dance

218
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:42,735
Please leave immediately

219
00:21:44,818 --> 00:21:47,519
Alright, hip-hop basics is starting!

220
00:21:47,574 --> 00:21:49,709
Follow me, push your neck out

221
00:21:49,710 --> 00:21:54,113
Pull it back, clap, clap, bend your knees

222
00:21:54,114 --> 00:21:56,215
Get the timing down

223
00:21:56,717 --> 00:21:58,673
Add the arms, speed up!

224
00:21:58,697 --> 00:22:00,920
Boom, boom, boom

225
00:22:00,921 --> 00:22:02,077
Don't forget your neck

226
00:22:02,101 --> 00:22:04,323
Boom, boom, boom

227
00:22:04,324 --> 00:22:07,660
Open your arms, tuck your neck, bend your knees

228
00:22:07,661 --> 00:22:10,463
Down, down, down, down, down

229
00:22:10,488 --> 00:22:12,081
Left, right, left

230
00:22:12,105 --> 00:22:15,192
Keep your body and shoulders facing the mirror

231
00:22:15,435 --> 00:22:18,004
Hey, dance properly!

232
00:22:19,473 --> 00:22:21,807
Professionals respect their contracts

233
00:22:22,009 --> 00:22:23,009
Go down now

234
00:22:23,034 --> 00:22:24,167
Yeah...

235
00:22:25,078 --> 00:22:26,646
Relax your body

236
00:22:31,952 --> 00:22:32,985
I'm done

237
00:22:35,706 --> 00:22:36,845
Keep dancing

238
00:22:36,869 --> 00:22:38,191
Come on, back to your spots

239
00:22:38,458 --> 00:22:40,426
Step back and find the beat

240
00:22:40,427 --> 00:22:42,962
Come on, your leg...
- Don't touch my leg

241
00:22:44,865 --> 00:22:45,832
Hey!

242
00:22:46,366 --> 00:22:47,934
Forget about those who don't want to dance

243
00:22:47,935 --> 00:22:49,035
Let's dance!

244
00:22:49,036 --> 00:22:52,605
Go! Boom, boom, turn right!

245
00:23:24,471 --> 00:23:25,260
Stand up

246
00:23:26,039 --> 00:23:27,139
Raise it

247
00:23:28,876 --> 00:23:30,068
Like this

248
00:23:30,092 --> 00:23:31,644
Raising it to here

249
00:23:31,845 --> 00:23:32,810
Heels forward!

250
00:23:33,126 --> 00:23:34,547
Heels further forward

251
00:23:34,915 --> 00:23:36,482
How many times do I have to tell you?

252
00:23:36,650 --> 00:23:38,584
Are you really my child?

253
00:23:38,819 --> 00:23:41,420
I've had enough!
- Daiya, wait

254
00:23:45,592 --> 00:23:47,560
Daiya, wait!

255
00:23:48,529 --> 00:23:49,996
Daiya, wait!

256
00:24:03,777 --> 00:24:05,144
Alright, start from the right

257
00:24:05,179 --> 00:24:07,613
Seven, eight, one, two...

258
00:24:08,415 --> 00:24:09,715
Start from the left

259
00:24:13,787 --> 00:24:15,021
I can't do this anymore

260
00:24:18,559 --> 00:24:19,792
Keep practicing

261
00:24:19,793 --> 00:24:21,260
Stop ordering me around!

262
00:24:21,962 --> 00:24:23,685
We have to form a team

263
00:24:24,298 --> 00:24:26,132
Don't mess this up

264
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:27,255
A team?

265
00:24:28,736 --> 00:24:30,236
Like I give a damn

266
00:24:30,871 --> 00:24:33,406
I've always worked alone

267
00:24:34,107 --> 00:24:36,275
You bastard

268
00:24:38,045 --> 00:24:40,580
yakuza

269
00:24:51,225 --> 00:24:55,228
Um, please don't come back here again

270
00:25:14,414 --> 00:25:15,515
Dai?

271
00:25:18,285 --> 00:25:19,585
Asuka!

272
00:25:24,424 --> 00:25:25,525
You two know each other?

273
00:25:25,959 --> 00:25:27,032
Uh...

274
00:25:27,056 --> 00:25:28,628
yeah, we do

275
00:25:29,796 --> 00:25:31,864
You seem a bit different than usual

276
00:25:37,204 --> 00:25:38,771
I do not

277
00:25:38,972 --> 00:25:41,974
Anyway, what are you doing here?

278
00:25:42,376 --> 00:25:44,944
I told you about my dream

279
00:25:45,112 --> 00:25:47,013
To be a dancer

280
00:25:47,281 --> 00:25:49,949
You're the one who told me to go after it

281
00:25:50,184 --> 00:25:52,852
Right, I did say that

282
00:25:53,487 --> 00:25:56,389
Are you guys here to learn to dance too?

283
00:25:56,390 --> 00:25:58,491
They're just passing by

284
00:25:58,492 --> 00:26:02,295
Little princess, we're just hopeless old guys

285
00:26:02,296 --> 00:26:06,199
that keep getting kicked out by the dance teachers

286
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:09,135
Do you know where we can learn?

287
00:26:09,136 --> 00:26:09,969
Hey!

288
00:26:10,737 --> 00:26:12,805
You all want to learn to dance?

289
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:15,041
I can teach you

290
00:26:15,042 --> 00:26:17,343
Really?
- Seriously?

291
00:26:17,811 --> 00:26:20,179
No, absolutely not

292
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:23,983
But can you actually dance?

293
00:26:53,380 --> 00:26:55,214
I don't mind showing you

294
00:26:55,424 --> 00:26:57,416
She's amazing!

295
00:26:58,051 --> 00:27:00,920
Right, Dai?

296
00:27:05,292 --> 00:27:08,594
Don't you want that 100 million yen?

297
00:27:23,944 --> 00:27:27,480
[Ezaki Community Center]

298
00:27:45,599 --> 00:27:46,632
Everyone, inside

299
00:28:10,624 --> 00:28:12,859
Alright, take off your sunglasses

300
00:28:22,002 --> 00:28:24,537
We're starting with smile training

301
00:28:24,705 --> 00:28:26,706
Come on, say cheese!

302
00:28:28,175 --> 00:28:33,012
Little princess, we came here to learn to dance

303
00:28:33,647 --> 00:28:35,381
Dancing starts with your expression

304
00:28:35,382 --> 00:28:37,149
And expressions start from the heart

305
00:28:37,684 --> 00:28:39,986
Your hearts aren't smiling at all

306
00:28:41,388 --> 00:28:44,190
Come on, cheese!

307
00:29:03,043 --> 00:29:04,900
First, the box step

308
00:29:04,924 --> 00:29:05,912
Watch me

309
00:29:17,324 --> 00:29:18,891
Now, you try

310
00:29:35,509 --> 00:29:36,943
Stop, stop!

311
00:29:37,611 --> 00:29:40,613
Uncle Kiryu do you actually want to practice?

312
00:29:43,217 --> 00:29:45,051
You look like you have some experience

313
00:29:45,235 --> 00:29:48,554
Maybe you're used to slacking off...

314
00:29:48,722 --> 00:29:50,389
but that won't fly with me

315
00:29:50,624 --> 00:29:53,626
You're adults so do it right

316
00:29:53,794 --> 00:29:55,461
And you're laughing?

317
00:29:55,896 --> 00:29:56,929
Sorry

318
00:29:58,031 --> 00:29:59,632
Alright, again

319
00:30:12,980 --> 00:30:13,913
It's me

320
00:30:17,885 --> 00:30:20,086
Turn off your phones during practice

321
00:30:20,921 --> 00:30:22,288
That's basic courtesy

322
00:30:24,591 --> 00:30:27,326
But I love oldies too, so you're forgiven

323
00:30:29,730 --> 00:30:31,097
Alright, again

324
00:31:12,706 --> 00:31:14,173
Okay, let's take a break

325
00:31:21,949 --> 00:31:22,982
I've decided

326
00:31:24,351 --> 00:31:25,484
Decided what?

327
00:31:26,153 --> 00:31:27,820
Your crew name

328
00:31:28,188 --> 00:31:30,957
A bizarre group like this has to be unique

329
00:31:30,958 --> 00:31:32,124
The Specials

330
00:31:33,390 --> 00:31:34,727
Isn't that a bit cheesy?

331
00:31:35,195 --> 00:31:37,452
I like it

332
00:31:37,961 --> 00:31:39,866
The Specials

333
00:31:40,167 --> 00:31:42,535
But I'd like one more member

334
00:31:42,736 --> 00:31:45,338
Then we could make a better formation

335
00:31:59,253 --> 00:32:02,488
Sorry for keeping you so late

336
00:32:02,923 --> 00:32:03,990
It's fine

337
00:32:07,861 --> 00:32:11,497
By the way, you seem different from your usual self

338
00:32:11,832 --> 00:32:14,100
Which one is the real you?

339
00:32:16,270 --> 00:32:17,670
They're both me

340
00:32:19,339 --> 00:32:21,741
Do you hate dancing?

341
00:32:23,177 --> 00:32:24,277
Huh?

342
00:32:25,112 --> 00:32:31,184
Because you look so miserable when you dance

343
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:36,088
Do I?

344
00:32:36,723 --> 00:32:39,358
Indecisive men aren't very charming

345
00:32:40,294 --> 00:32:41,049
Right

346
00:32:41,073 --> 00:32:42,461
Sorry

347
00:32:43,463 --> 00:32:44,797
You're back!
- I'm home

348
00:32:44,989 --> 00:32:45,984
Welcome back!

349
00:32:46,008 --> 00:32:48,034
I bought delicious donuts

350
00:32:48,035 --> 00:32:49,936
Really?
- Go wash your hands, everyone

351
00:32:51,605 --> 00:32:53,472
Hurry up, Dai

352
00:33:10,924 --> 00:33:12,758
I heard you're making a comeback

353
00:33:13,227 --> 00:33:14,961
What are you talking about?

354
00:33:17,064 --> 00:33:22,802
Just remember, we haven't forgiven you

355
00:33:45,792 --> 00:33:48,253
Still scrubbing, old man?

356
00:33:49,046 --> 00:33:50,329
It's still dirty

357
00:33:50,330 --> 00:33:51,640
Look over there

358
00:33:51,664 --> 00:33:52,665
Wipe it properly

359
00:33:52,666 --> 00:33:54,060
Scrubbing every day...

360
00:33:54,084 --> 00:33:55,935
Tough life

361
00:33:56,270 --> 00:33:57,870
Make sure you get it clean

362
00:34:00,641 --> 00:34:02,041
Clean it right

363
00:34:03,810 --> 00:34:04,944
No answer?

364
00:34:06,390 --> 00:34:07,647
I got it

365
00:34:07,648 --> 00:34:08,714
Good

366
00:34:10,117 --> 00:34:12,818
We're counting on you, old man

367
00:34:30,304 --> 00:34:31,337
Big Brother

368
00:34:37,644 --> 00:34:39,544
Kumashiro?

369
00:34:40,681 --> 00:34:42,381
Long time no see

370
00:34:44,585 --> 00:34:46,719
You look well

371
00:34:48,822 --> 00:34:50,723
Don't say a word

372
00:34:52,993 --> 00:34:57,062
A yakuza enforcer fresh out of prison like me...

373
00:34:57,498 --> 00:34:59,398
can only end up in a place like this

374
00:35:06,240 --> 00:35:10,109
Actually, I have a job for you

375
00:35:11,712 --> 00:35:15,915
But I'll tell you upfront, I can't guarantee you'll survive

376
00:35:27,628 --> 00:35:28,283
Hey!

377
00:35:28,307 --> 00:35:29,441
We're talking to you

378
00:35:30,364 --> 00:35:31,964
Why are you slacking off?

379
00:35:31,965 --> 00:35:34,233
Didn't we tell you to clean it properly?

380
00:35:38,705 --> 00:35:39,939
I'm sorry

381
00:35:40,874 --> 00:35:42,027
Hey, boys

382
00:35:42,776 --> 00:35:45,144
Can I borrow him for a bit?

383
00:35:45,169 --> 00:35:46,025
What?

384
00:35:46,481 --> 00:35:48,071
Who the hell are you?

385
00:35:58,759 --> 00:36:00,282
If I tell you my name,

386
00:36:01,361 --> 00:36:04,163
can you handle the heat?

387
00:36:11,673 --> 00:36:12,772
I'm sorry

388
00:36:13,379 --> 00:36:14,196
Please

389
00:36:15,142 --> 00:36:16,348
Go right ahead

390
00:36:23,617 --> 00:36:24,617
This way please

391
00:36:37,764 --> 00:36:42,101
This reminds me of our time in prison

392
00:36:42,436 --> 00:36:43,379
Yeah

393
00:36:44,638 --> 00:36:46,639
We belonged to different families...

394
00:36:46,974 --> 00:36:50,042
but I've always looked up to you as a big brother

395
00:36:54,340 --> 00:36:55,136
So?

396
00:36:56,583 --> 00:36:58,676
What's the job?

397
00:37:00,854 --> 00:37:02,221
Dancing

398
00:37:04,691 --> 00:37:06,292
Dancing...

399
00:37:12,032 --> 00:37:13,232
Dancing?

400
00:37:16,503 --> 00:37:17,526
Didn't you say...

401
00:37:18,472 --> 00:37:22,675
you learned to dance when you were young?

402
00:37:26,587 --> 00:37:28,187
It was Bon Odori (Japanese folk dance)

403
00:37:31,852 --> 00:37:34,854
Bon Odori?

404
00:37:37,090 --> 00:37:38,224
Yes

405
00:37:41,328 --> 00:37:46,065
Well, dance is dance

406
00:37:53,674 --> 00:37:55,408
Drive

407
00:38:07,120 --> 00:38:11,123
I'm the new guy, Murasame

408
00:38:12,226 --> 00:38:14,527
Hope you'll take care of me

409
00:38:16,029 --> 00:38:17,430
Another yakuza?

410
00:38:20,300 --> 00:38:21,534
What?

411
00:38:22,736 --> 00:38:25,238
Kid, what did you just say?

412
00:38:25,239 --> 00:38:27,640
You want to fight?

413
00:38:32,079 --> 00:38:33,646
No fighting

414
00:38:38,752 --> 00:38:40,753
Nice to meet you, Gramps

415
00:38:42,256 --> 00:38:43,623
Gramps?

416
00:39:10,651 --> 00:39:11,817
Let's stop here

417
00:39:43,050 --> 00:39:44,116
Hey, Princess!

418
00:39:46,153 --> 00:39:47,553
Where are we?

419
00:39:47,821 --> 00:39:49,956
Today, we're going on a warrior-training trip!

420
00:39:50,357 --> 00:39:52,024
Warrior training?

421
00:39:52,659 --> 00:39:53,528
No more questions

422
00:39:53,552 --> 00:39:54,126
Let's go

423
00:39:59,633 --> 00:40:01,734
There's a dance battle happening here

424
00:40:02,369 --> 00:40:03,925
Anyone can join

425
00:40:03,949 --> 00:40:05,238
Perfect for you guys, right?

426
00:40:05,806 --> 00:40:08,374
Kids shouldn't be in a place like this

427
00:40:08,575 --> 00:40:09,842
It's fine during the day

428
00:40:10,010 --> 00:40:11,577
Excuse me

429
00:40:12,346 --> 00:40:13,513
Asuka!

430
00:40:13,514 --> 00:40:15,648
Yeah!
- Yeah!

431
00:40:17,684 --> 00:40:22,221
Do you know what you're missing?

432
00:40:22,756 --> 00:40:23,612
What?

433
00:40:24,194 --> 00:40:25,058
Do you know?

434
00:40:25,083 --> 00:40:26,392
No

435
00:40:26,417 --> 00:40:29,061
You're too stupid to know anyway

436
00:40:29,062 --> 00:40:30,263
You bastard

437
00:40:30,264 --> 00:40:31,397
Stop fighting

438
00:40:32,699 --> 00:40:33,655
Passion

439
00:40:34,038 --> 00:40:35,168
Enthusiasm

440
00:40:35,702 --> 00:40:38,070
Even if you suck, you have to enjoy it

441
00:40:38,539 --> 00:40:39,705
Alright, let's go

442
00:40:47,347 --> 00:40:49,782
We need more dancers!

443
00:40:52,085 --> 00:40:54,556
Okay, next up is Tomo's performance!

444
00:40:54,580 --> 00:40:56,055
Here we go!

445
00:41:19,913 --> 00:41:22,715
Thank you, Tomo!

446
00:41:25,485 --> 00:41:26,601
Asuka, long time no see!

447
00:41:26,625 --> 00:41:27,420
How have you been?

448
00:41:27,421 --> 00:41:30,957
Three, two, one, go!

449
00:41:49,409 --> 00:41:53,479
Let's go, Roora!

450
00:41:53,614 --> 00:41:57,650
Now, is there anyone else who wants to dance?

451
00:41:59,686 --> 00:42:02,955
Let's welcome the king of dance!

452
00:42:03,190 --> 00:42:06,292
Come on, get up here
- Come on!

453
00:42:06,293 --> 00:42:08,094
Alright, don't hesitate!

454
00:42:45,499 --> 00:42:46,659
Thank you!

455
00:42:46,683 --> 00:42:48,427
That Bon Odori was amazing!

456
00:42:48,451 --> 00:42:49,969
Who's next?

457
00:42:49,970 --> 00:42:51,804
No, I really can't do this

458
00:42:51,805 --> 00:42:55,208
You got this!
- I can't dance to this music

459
00:42:58,145 --> 00:42:58,978
Hey!

460
00:42:59,546 --> 00:43:00,646
Sister

461
00:43:01,315 --> 00:43:02,148
What is it?

462
00:43:02,182 --> 00:43:03,883
I want to ask you a favor

463
00:43:07,521 --> 00:43:10,156
No, no, absolutely not!

464
00:43:10,157 --> 00:43:11,557
No means no!

465
00:43:20,267 --> 00:43:24,937
♪ Iyo is still 16... ♪

466
00:43:24,938 --> 00:43:27,507
♪ Only 16! ♪

467
00:43:27,508 --> 00:43:31,711
♪ Swayed by temptations... ♪

468
00:43:32,246 --> 00:43:36,749
♪ and led astray by you... ♪

469
00:43:37,184 --> 00:43:41,787
♪ A sentimental journey ♪

470
00:43:44,224 --> 00:43:46,792
The Showa era really brings back memories

471
00:43:47,094 --> 00:43:48,060
Incredible

472
00:44:00,874 --> 00:44:02,308
Lastly, we'll leave it to you

473
00:44:02,309 --> 00:44:04,210
Give it your all with the ballet!

474
00:44:24,064 --> 00:44:26,065
Yeah, nice moves!

475
00:44:37,945 --> 00:44:39,601
What's wrong with him?

476
00:44:39,625 --> 00:44:42,148
Anyone want to step in?

477
00:44:42,149 --> 00:44:45,017
Sorry, I still can't do it

478
00:44:45,752 --> 00:44:47,687
All you guys ever say is no

479
00:44:47,955 --> 00:44:49,856
But you've practiced so much

480
00:44:50,324 --> 00:44:53,526
But I just can't dance in front of people

481
00:44:53,527 --> 00:44:55,495
It doesn't matter if you aren't perfect

482
00:44:55,762 --> 00:44:57,463
Just show your true self

483
00:44:57,464 --> 00:44:59,165
and dance freely

484
00:44:59,766 --> 00:45:02,935
You're adults, why back down before even trying?

485
00:45:12,813 --> 00:45:15,314
Asuka's hitting the dance floor!

486
00:45:41,375 --> 00:45:44,810
If you don't change, I'm out of ideas

487
00:45:46,980 --> 00:45:47,980
Asuka!

488
00:45:51,351 --> 00:45:52,518
I told you!

489
00:45:53,554 --> 00:45:55,888
People like us just can't dance

490
00:45:57,324 --> 00:45:59,592
Let alone form a team

491
00:46:00,827 --> 00:46:03,729
Thank you for your wonderful performances today

492
00:46:03,730 --> 00:46:06,504
Alright, everyone, let's keep the energy up!

493
00:46:06,528 --> 00:46:08,034
Let's go!

494
00:46:17,010 --> 00:46:18,344
Asuka!

495
00:46:19,746 --> 00:46:22,782
Excuse me, have you seen a girl about this tall?

496
00:46:23,917 --> 00:46:24,851
Thanks

497
00:46:25,953 --> 00:46:27,042
Asuka!

498
00:46:27,407 --> 00:46:28,433
Asuka!

499
00:46:30,924 --> 00:46:32,013
Asuka!

500
00:46:32,459 --> 00:46:33,626
Asuka!

501
00:46:38,265 --> 00:46:40,867
Damn it, Asuka

502
00:46:41,034 --> 00:46:43,870
Kids that age are so difficult

503
00:46:44,972 --> 00:46:46,272
Leave me alone

504
00:46:46,473 --> 00:46:48,975
She's important to me too

505
00:46:50,978 --> 00:46:52,078
Princess!

506
00:46:54,748 --> 00:46:55,982
Asuka!

507
00:47:12,733 --> 00:47:14,600
They were targeting you

508
00:47:15,836 --> 00:47:17,136
What is this about?

509
00:47:17,337 --> 00:47:18,304
Who knows

510
00:47:20,774 --> 00:47:23,776
Looks like you haven't lost your touch

511
00:47:27,080 --> 00:47:28,147
Who's he?

512
00:47:30,417 --> 00:47:31,918
My former employer

513
00:47:31,919 --> 00:47:33,653
You traitor!

514
00:48:29,810 --> 00:48:31,177
What are you doing?

515
00:48:34,481 --> 00:48:35,237
Back off

516
00:48:35,581 --> 00:48:36,550
I'll handle this

517
00:49:12,553 --> 00:49:16,022
She's that corrupt politician's daughter

518
00:49:17,891 --> 00:49:20,860
She's grown up so much

519
00:49:59,566 --> 00:50:00,299
Get back!

520
00:50:47,347 --> 00:50:50,016
But you can't escape the organization

521
00:50:52,519 --> 00:50:55,888
I look forward to our next meeting

522
00:51:05,065 --> 00:51:08,201
(Dai, sorry I went home ahead of you.)

523
00:51:14,074 --> 00:51:15,074
She went home

524
00:51:18,212 --> 00:51:21,714
Kumashiro sent you to appease us didn't he?

525
00:51:24,084 --> 00:51:25,718
I was asked by him

526
00:51:28,255 --> 00:51:31,490
But I simply wanted to have a drink with you

527
00:51:32,192 --> 00:51:34,694
An old guy with not much time left is begging you

528
00:51:34,862 --> 00:51:36,729
At least keep me company

529
00:51:38,432 --> 00:51:40,099
What a strange man

530
00:51:41,034 --> 00:51:43,069
What's your relationship with Kumashiro?

531
00:51:44,238 --> 00:51:47,540
We were cellmates in prison

532
00:51:49,209 --> 00:51:51,777
That's why I wanted to help him

533
00:51:51,778 --> 00:51:53,679
So you'd do anything for him?

534
00:51:54,748 --> 00:51:56,048
How cliché

535
00:51:57,784 --> 00:51:59,237
I

536
00:52:00,664 --> 00:52:03,022
would die for Kumashiro

537
00:52:03,357 --> 00:52:04,357
How boring

538
00:52:04,358 --> 00:52:06,559
Why would you die for someone else?

539
00:52:08,436 --> 00:52:09,462
Let's put it this way

540
00:52:11,865 --> 00:52:12,687
You're too far

541
00:52:14,104 --> 00:52:14,967
Come closer!

542
00:52:19,873 --> 00:52:24,243
Aren't we supposed to be partners?

543
00:52:30,450 --> 00:52:32,919
Welcome, boss!

544
00:52:32,920 --> 00:52:33,786
Did you cut your hair?

545
00:52:35,088 --> 00:52:37,657
Hey, look

546
00:52:37,658 --> 00:52:40,826
There's a washed-up gangster drinking

547
00:52:41,094 --> 00:52:42,929
I never want to end up like that

548
00:52:44,565 --> 00:52:45,431
What's your problem?

549
00:52:46,600 --> 00:52:47,633
Don't

550
00:52:47,634 --> 00:52:51,904
Please sit, sit down

551
00:52:51,905 --> 00:52:52,857
We're sorry about that

552
00:52:52,881 --> 00:52:53,573
You okay?

553
00:52:53,574 --> 00:52:56,108
Why didn't you fight back?

554
00:52:59,012 --> 00:53:01,747
Because some things are more important than fighting

555
00:53:05,686 --> 00:53:08,588
Anyway, let's not talk about that

556
00:53:08,822 --> 00:53:10,690
That running dance the princess taught us...

557
00:53:10,691 --> 00:53:11,924
It's the Running Man

558
00:53:12,826 --> 00:53:15,828
Right, that's the one

559
00:53:18,866 --> 00:53:21,634
Should our feet be about this wide?

560
00:53:27,941 --> 00:53:28,975
For that move...

561
00:53:29,476 --> 00:53:34,441
you go like this, then like this

562
00:53:35,015 --> 00:53:38,651
And then, you do this

563
00:53:39,219 --> 00:53:40,353
After that, like this

564
00:53:40,354 --> 00:53:41,988
Like this?

565
00:53:41,989 --> 00:53:43,356
No, it isn't
- What?

566
00:53:43,657 --> 00:53:44,657
Move aside

567
00:53:45,459 --> 00:53:46,392
Like this?

568
00:53:51,798 --> 00:53:53,566
You're actually pretty good

569
00:53:55,426 --> 00:53:56,375
You went too fast

570
00:53:56,399 --> 00:53:57,303
Show me again

571
00:53:57,304 --> 00:53:58,894
Show me again, come on!

572
00:53:58,918 --> 00:54:00,573
Step over here

573
00:54:00,574 --> 00:54:04,177
Show me one more time

574
00:54:04,178 --> 00:54:11,484
Ready, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

575
00:54:17,524 --> 00:54:18,691
So cool

576
00:54:21,762 --> 00:54:23,429
You seem to be enjoying yourself, old man

577
00:54:23,430 --> 00:54:27,567
Yeah, dancing is actually quite fun

578
00:54:29,169 --> 00:54:30,770
So cool

579
00:54:35,175 --> 00:54:37,210
Your expression has softened

580
00:54:39,046 --> 00:54:40,012
Mom

581
00:54:40,414 --> 00:54:41,681
What is it?

582
00:54:42,883 --> 00:54:44,617
I started dancing again

583
00:54:47,087 --> 00:54:48,421
Oh?

584
00:54:48,789 --> 00:54:50,389
